---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const entries = [
  {
    date: "2026-11-13",
    items: [
      "ZBLL finder: after picking the shape, tap the colors you see on your cube and it narrows down to your case, usually in five or six taps. Tested on every case from every angle and coloring.",
      "ZBLL: every case of a shape is now drawn from the same angle, so the pictures line up with each other and with your cube. Some algorithms start with a U turn because of this; case numbers and algorithms are unchanged.",
      "ZBLL finder: the 21 PLLs are named and listed by name, arrows show where pieces need to go, cases are drawn from the angle where the fewest pieces move, and a note explains that your colors may differ from the pictures.",
      "Added six more example solves (37–39 moves, about 8.3–8.6 s), each replayed on a simulated cube, with a summary table and links to every EODFDB and ZBLL case.",
      "Fixed the intuitive EODFDB instructions: before the final M2 the centers must be upside down, not aligned.",
      "Roux comparison: step-by-step models for both intuitive steps under three tie rules (lookahead, no lookahead, worst), with per-step averages that add up. EODFDB is split into three steps like LSE (the earlier two-step split was close to optimal by construction). Result: about even in moves for a typical solver; solved well, Roux takes about 1.4 fewer.",
      "EODFDB is now taught in three steps: orient, bring the bottom edges up, M2.",
      "Said per set how the computed algorithm lists compare with human ones, and that both algorithm averages are weighted.",
      "Added a trainer for EODFDB and ZBLL.",
      "Added a ZBLL recognition guide, with computed data: the top face plus two adjacent sides always identifies the case; one side never does.",
      "Learning path rewritten with algorithm counts for every stage and how often each ZBLL set comes up.",
      "Added a printable one-page cheat sheet for the 46-case EODFDB set.",
      "Recognition guide: fixed the top-face-only figure (no view identifies a case, not 4%), committed every view to the script, and tested the taught pattern words: they narrow the case down but don't pick it alone.",
      "Learning path: counts now mean algorithms in your final set (539 at most), frequencies are labeled as share of solves, and group sizes fit H and PLL.",
      "Recognition guide wording: the three looks narrow the case down and the colors pick it; no speed claim without timing data.",
    ],
  },
  {
    date: "2026-11-12",
    items: [
      "Added a computed CMLL list (42 cases), generated with the same search as ZBLL, so the Roux comparison uses like-for-like numbers.",
      "Roux comparison: turns of the top layer counted the same way on both sides; Roux about 21.4, ZBRoux about 22.9.",
      "EODFDB cases are shown from the angle where their shortest solution starts, so no algorithm begins with a turn of the top layer. 422 cases got one move shorter.",
      "Mirror pairs are shown from reflected angles; a mirror's algorithm is exactly the original with U and U' swapped.",
      "Added the 46-case EODFDB set with its definition, the Burnside derivation of the case counts, and per-case and per-position averages.",
      "Added downloadable JSON and CSV data, this changelog, and a who-should-use-it section.",
      "Licensed the algorithm data under CC BY 4.0 and the code under MIT.",
    ],
  },
  {
    date: "2026-11-11",
    items: [
      "First version: ZBRoux guide, EODFDB case finder (992 cases), ZBLL lists and finder (493 cases), LEOR EOStripe case lists and solver.",
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base title="Changelog" description="What has changed on the ZBRoux Wiki and in its data.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Changelog</h1>
    <p class="lede">Changes to the pages and to the algorithm data, newest first. The full history is in the <a href="https://github.com/VKSFY/zbroux-wiki/commits/main">repository</a>.</p>
    {entries.map((e) => (
      <section>
        <h2>{e.date}</h2>
        <ul>{e.items.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul>
      </section>
    ))}
  </article>
</Base>
